_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 31
---
order: 31
---
short_label: III.31
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: In a circle the angle in the semicircle is right, that in a greater segment less than a right angle, and that in a less segment greater than a right angle; further the angle of the greater segment is greater than a right angle, and the angle of the less segment is less than a right angle.
----
proof:

Let *ABCD* be a circle, let *BC* be its diameter, and *E* its center.  Join *BA, AC, AD,* and *DC.*

I say that the angle *BAC* in the semicircle *BAC* is right, the angle *ABC* in the segment *ABC* greater than the semicircle is less than a right angle, and the angle *ADC* in the segment *ADC* less than the semicircle is greater than a right angle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="III.31 diagram" src="propIII31.gif"/></noscript>
